{"name":"White Castle","hex":"#dbd5d1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"White Castle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The first fast-food hamburger chain and one of the oldest American fast-food restaurant chains, known for its Slyder, a small square burger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/White_Castle"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Castle, Monmouthshire","blocks":[{"text":"White Castle, also known historically as Llantilio Castle, is a ruined castle near the village of Llantilio Crossenny in Monmouthshire, Wales. The fortification was established by the Normans in the wake of the invasion of England in 1066, to protect the route from Wales to Hereford. Possibly commissioned by William fitz Osbern, the Earl of Hereford, it comprised three large earthworks with timber defences. In 1135, a major Welsh revolt took place and in response King Stephen brought together White Castle and its sister fortifications of Grosmont and Skenfrith to form a lordship known as the \"Three Castles\", which continued to play a role in defending the region from Welsh attack for several centuries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg/330px-White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Castle%2C_Monmouthshire"},{"title":"White Castle (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"White Castle is an American regional hamburger restaurant chain with about 345 locations across 13 states, with its greatest presence in the Midwest and New York metropolitan area. It was founded in 1921, in Wichita, Kansas. White Castle has been generally credited as the world's first fast food hamburger chain. It is known for its small, square hamburgers – commonly referred to as \"sliders\" – sold at low prices: five cents from their introduction while gradually increasing in price during the 1930s, with promotional coupons in the 1940s, offering five burgers for ten cents. In 2014, Time named the White Castle slider \"The Most Influential Burger of All Time\". The company's restaurant locations are white buildings decorated with a castle motif."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e1/White_Castle_logo.svg/330px-White_Castle_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Castle_(restaurant)"},{"title":"Castle","blocks":[{"text":"A castle is a type of fortified structure built during the Middle Ages predominantly by the nobility or royalty and by military orders. Scholars usually consider a castle to be the private fortified residence of a lord or noble. This is distinct from a mansion, palace, and villa, whose main purpose was exclusively for pleasance and are not primarily fortresses but may be fortified. Use of the term has varied over time and, sometimes, has also been applied to structures such as hill forts and 19th- and 20th-century homes built to resemble castles. Over the Middle Ages, when genuine castles were built, they took on a great many forms with many different features, although some, such as curtain walls, arrowslits, and portcullises, were commonplace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Panor%C3%A1mica_Oto%C3%B1o_Alc%C3%A1zar_de_Segovia.jpg/330px-Panor%C3%A1mica_Oto%C3%B1o_Alc%C3%A1zar_de_Segovia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg/500px-White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg/1280px-White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg/500px-White_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_Castle%2C_Cadw_image.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/The_ruins_of_White_Castle_on_a_gloomy_October_day_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1007095.jpg/500px-The_ruins_of_White_Castle_on_a_gloomy_October_day_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1007095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/The_ruins_of_White_Castle_on_a_gloomy_October_day_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1007095.jpg/500px-The_ruins_of_White_Castle_on_a_gloomy_October_day_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1007095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The outer ward's gatehouse","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_ruins_of_White_Castle_on_a_gloomy_October_day_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1007095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg/500px-White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg/1280px-White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg/500px-White_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The castle's unusual arrow loops","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_Castle%2C_arrow_slit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/White_Castle%2C_inner_ward.JPG/500px-White_Castle%2C_inner_ward.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_